{"id": "xtaiwan", "name": "Yushan National Park", "short": "Yushan", "place": "Taiwan", "lat": 23.47, "lon": 120.96, "side": "r", "cont": "Asia", "country": "Taiwan", "kind": "Polar & mountain", "park": true, "blurb": "Taiwan's highest peaks: oak and hemlock forest, deer, bears and hawk-eagles.", "tip": {"id": "oak", "title": "Thin the oak mast", "text": "Oak acorns feed boar, squirrels, rodents and bears. Cut Oaks by 50% and watch those eaters, then the marten, weasel, hawk-eagle and bear that depend on them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Yushan National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yushan_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Formosan black bear", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Formosan_black_bear"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Mountain hawk-eagle", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_hawk-eagle"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Formosan serow", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Formosan_serow"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Formosan rock macaque", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Formosan_rock_macaque"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Yellow-throated marten", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow-throated_marten"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Yushan National Park", "icon": "ice", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "Sunlight drives growth from the warm lowland forests up to the cold alpine zone. Cloud and mist often cut it back on the slopes."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "monsoon and typhoon rain", "xh": 0.4}, {"id": "cold", "sp": "cold and winter snow", "xh": 0.68}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.92, "name": "Fungi and soil microbes", "desc": "Break down fallen leaves, cones, wood and carcasses, returning nutrients to the mountai